# PART 2: FIX THE OPTIONAL ASSESSMENT TIME LIMIT

## 2.1 Existing problem

In the assessment settings, tutors can decide whether an assessment should have a time limit.

There is a checkbox for setting a time limit, alongside the field where the tutor specifies the duration.

However, even when the tutor leaves the time-limit checkbox unchecked, students still see a default 30-minute countdown when attempting the assessment.

This should not happen.

## 2.2 Required behaviour

The time limit must be genuinely optional.

**When the tutor does not enable the time limit:**

- Do not display a countdown timer to the student.
- Do not display the default 30-minute timer.
- Do not silently apply a default duration.
- The assessment must not automatically close because of a time limit that the tutor never configured.
- Students should be able to complete and submit the assessment according to its other configured rules.

**When the tutor enables the time limit:**

- Display the configured countdown timer to the student.
- Use the exact duration specified by the tutor.
- Enforce the configured duration correctly.
- Automatically handle assessment expiry according to the existing assessment submission rules.

The timer should only become visible when a valid time limit has explicitly been enabled and saved by the tutor.

## 2.3 Acceptance criteria

| Tutor configuration | Student experience |
|---|---|
| Time limit disabled | No countdown timer |
| Time limit enabled: 30 minutes | 30-minute countdown |
| Time limit enabled: 60 minutes | 60-minute countdown |
| Time limit enabled: any other valid duration | Display and enforce that duration |

Do not let frontend defaults override the tutor's saved configuration.

