# PART 3: MAKE PASSCODES MANDATORY FOR TESTS AND EXAMINATIONS

## 3.1 Required behaviour

The assessment system supports different types of work, including activities, assignments, tests, and examinations.

Passcodes should not be mandatory for ordinary activities and assignments.

However, **tests and examinations must always require a passcode**.

Implement the following rules:

| Assessment type | Passcode requirement |
|---|---|
| Activity | Optional / not required by default |
| Assignment | Optional / not required by default |
| Test | Mandatory |
| Examination | Mandatory |

When a tutor selects Test or Examination as the assessment type:

1. Automatically enable the passcode requirement.
2. Keep the passcode checkbox checked.
3. Disable the checkbox so the tutor cannot turn the requirement off.
4. Ensure the system enforces the requirement on the backend as well.

The tutor should not be able to publish a test or examination without a valid passcode configuration.

For activities and assignments, preserve the existing flexibility.

